    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1028">

                <pb facs="1162" n="1152" sameAs="frus:frus1944v04/pg1152"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">861.24/11–644</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Assistant Secretary of State</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Acheson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Chairman of
                        the Government Purchasing Commission of the Soviet Union in the United
                        States</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Rudenko</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-11-07">November 7,
                        1944</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear General Rudenko</hi>: With reference to our
                    conversation of November 6 and the letter from Mr. Stepanov which you handed to
                    me at that time, you will find enclosed a reply to Mr. Stepanov which I would
                    appreciate your delivering to him. As agreed between us, I am communicating with
                    our Embassy in Moscow, asking them to give the same information to Mr.
                    Stepanov.</p>
                <p>Sincerely yours,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Dean Acheson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>


                <xi:include href="d1028-a1.xml" xpointer="d1028-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
